### 1.3 Critical Issues

> [!CAUTION]
> **CRIT-DB-01: `email` is nullable on `candidates` but used as duplicate-detection key.**
> [ATSScanner.tsx L324](file:///c:/Users/veere/Downloads/Task-Flow-Tracker-hackathon/Task-Flow-Tracker-hackathon/flowtracker/src/pages/hr/recruitment/ATSScanner.tsx#L324) inserts candidates with `email: null`. [JobApplication.tsx L135](file:///c:/Users/veere/Downloads/Task-Flow-Tracker-hackathon/Task-Flow-Tracker-hackathon/flowtracker/src/pages/public/JobApplication.tsx#L135) uses `.eq("email", cleanEmail)` to deduplicate. But NULL != NULL in SQL, so every null-email candidate creates a new record. Result: **unbounded duplicates** for every resume uploaded without an extractable email.

> [!CAUTION]
> **CRIT-DB-02: `candidates` and `profiles` are disconnected.**
> External candidates exist in `candidates`. Internal employees exist in `profiles`. When a candidate is onboarded, [OnboardingCenter.tsx L172](file:///c:/Users/veere/Downloads/Task-Flow-Tracker-hackathon/Task-Flow-Tracker-hackathon/flowtracker/src/pages/hr/OnboardingCenter.tsx#L172) creates a new `profiles` entry via `supabase.auth.admin.createUser()`, but the `candidates` record is never linked to the new `profiles` record. There is **no FK between candidates and profiles**.

> [!CAUTION]
> **CRIT-DB-03: Candidate `stage` field is overwritten globally, not per-application.**
> When a candidate applies to multiple jobs, [JobApplication.tsx L333](file:///c:/Users/veere/Downloads/Task-Flow-Tracker-hackathon/Task-Flow-Tracker-hackathon/flowtracker/src/pages/public/JobApplication.tsx#L333) calls `supabase.from("candidates").update({ stage: finalPipelineStatus }).eq("id", candidateRecordId)`. This overwrites the global stage regardless of which job triggered the change. If a candidate is "Interview Cleared" for Job A and then applies for Job B (going to "Screening"), their stage is retroactively changed to "Screening" across all views.

