### 2.2 Critical Schema Conflicts

> [!CAUTION]
> **CRIT-DB-04: THREE tables track the same application event.**
>
> When a candidate submits a job application via [JobApplication.tsx](file:///c:/Users/veere/Downloads/Task-Flow-Tracker-hackathon/Task-Flow-Tracker-hackathon/flowtracker/src/pages/public/JobApplication.tsx), data is written to:
> 1. `job_applications` — the raw submission (L248-262)
> 2. `candidate_applications` — the tracking copy (L316-326)
> 3. `candidates` — stage update (L330-334)
>
> These three writes have **no transactional guarantee**. If write #2 fails after #1 succeeds, the application exists in `job_applications` but is invisible in `candidate_applications`, which is the table that [CandidatePipeline.tsx](file:///c:/Users/veere/Downloads/Task-Flow-Tracker-hackathon/Task-Flow-Tracker-hackathon/flowtracker/src/pages/hr/recruitment/CandidatePipeline.tsx) reads from.

> [!CAUTION]
> **CRIT-DB-05: `form_id` vs `job_form_id` — split-brain FK naming.**
>
> The same foreign key is called different names in different tables and modules:
>
> | Context | Column Name Used | File |
> |---------|-----------------|------|
> | `job_applications` INSERT | `form_id` | [JobApplication.tsx L251](file:///c:/Users/veere/Downloads/Task-Flow-Tracker-hackathon/Task-Flow-Tracker-hackathon/flowtracker/src/pages/public/JobApplication.tsx#L251) |
> | `job_applications` READ | `app.form_id \|\| app.job_form_id` | [ApplicationHub.tsx L78](file:///c:/Users/veere/Downloads/Task-Flow-Tracker-hackathon/Task-Flow-Tracker-hackathon/flowtracker/src/pages/hr/ApplicationHub.tsx#L78) |
> | `candidate_applications` INSERT | `job_form_id` | [JobApplication.tsx L319](file:///c:/Users/veere/Downloads/Task-Flow-Tracker-hackathon/Task-Flow-Tracker-hackathon/flowtracker/src/pages/public/JobApplication.tsx#L319) |
> | `candidate_applications` JOIN | `job_forms(job_title)` via FK | [CandidatePipeline.tsx L59](file:///c:/Users/veere/Downloads/Task-Flow-Tracker-hackathon/Task-Flow-Tracker-hackathon/flowtracker/src/pages/hr/recruitment/CandidatePipeline.tsx#L59) |
> | `job_applications` UPDATE | `.eq("form_id", jobFormId)` | [InterviewCenter.tsx L215](file:///c:/Users/veere/Downloads/Task-Flow-Tracker-hackathon/Task-Flow-Tracker-hackathon/flowtracker/src/pages/hr/recruitment/InterviewCenter.tsx#L215) |
> | `recruitment_posts` READ | `job_form_id` | [Careers.tsx L41](file:///c:/Users/veere/Downloads/Task-Flow-Tracker-hackathon/Task-Flow-Tracker-hackathon/flowtracker/src/pages/candidate/Careers.tsx#L41) |
>
> This means some `job_applications` rows have `form_id` populated but `job_form_id` NULL, and vice versa.

