### 3.2 Critical Issues

> [!CAUTION]
> **CRIT-DB-06: `assessment_tokens` has conflicting column schemas.**
>
> From [ApplicationHub.tsx L147-154](file:///c:/Users/veere/Downloads/Task-Flow-Tracker-hackathon/Task-Flow-Tracker-hackathon/flowtracker/src/pages/hr/ApplicationHub.tsx#L147):
> ```typescript
> .insert([{ candidate_id, assessment_id, token, used: false }])
> ```
> From [JobApplication.tsx L284-291](file:///c:/Users/veere/Downloads/Task-Flow-Tracker-hackathon/Task-Flow-Tracker-hackathon/flowtracker/src/pages/public/JobApplication.tsx#L284):
> ```typescript
> .insert([{ assessment_id, candidate_id, token, status: "Active", expires_at }])
> ```
> From [AssessmentCenter.tsx L261-264](file:///c:/Users/veere/Downloads/Task-Flow-Tracker-hackathon/Task-Flow-Tracker-hackathon/flowtracker/src/pages/hr/recruitment/AssessmentCenter.tsx#L261):
> ```typescript
> .select("*, assessments(*)").eq("token", ...).in("status", ["Active", "InProgress"])
> ```
>
> Three callers use three different column sets. The table likely has both `used` (BOOLEAN) and `status` (TEXT) columns, meaning some tokens track state via `used=true` and others via `status="Completed"`. These are **never reconciled**.

> [!WARNING]
> **HIGH-DB-02: `assessments` table stores correct answers alongside questions in JSONB.**
>
> The [AssessmentCenter.tsx L216-228](file:///c:/Users/veere/Downloads/Task-Flow-Tracker-hackathon/Task-Flow-Tracker-hackathon/flowtracker/src/pages/hr/recruitment/AssessmentCenter.tsx#L216) stores the entire question set — including `correctAnswer` — in a single `questions` JSONB column. While the frontend strips `correctAnswer` before displaying to candidates (L276-278), any user with database read access (via the anon key with no RLS) can `SELECT questions FROM assessments` and read all correct answers.

> [!WARNING]
> **HIGH-DB-03: No `application_id` linking between assessments and job applications.**
>
> Assessment tokens have `candidate_id` and `assessment_id` but the link to a **specific application** is inconsistent. [AssessmentCenter.tsx L285-286](file:///c:/Users/veere/Downloads/Task-Flow-Tracker-hackathon/Task-Flow-Tracker-hackathon/flowtracker/src/pages/hr/recruitment/AssessmentCenter.tsx#L285) reads `application_id` and `attempt_id` from the token, but [JobApplication.tsx](file:///c:/Users/veere/Downloads/Task-Flow-Tracker-hackathon/Task-Flow-Tracker-hackathon/flowtracker/src/pages/public/JobApplication.tsx#L284) never inserts these columns.

